Bot: RVR & JC College provides separate hostel facilities for boys and girls, accommodating nearly 1250 boys and 650 girls across all years. The boys' hostel, NES Mens Hostel, is located adjacent to the college campus at Chandramoulipuram, Chowdavaram, Guntur-522019, with two blocks: Block-I (123 rooms, 520 students) and Block-II (151 rooms, 730 students). The girls' hostel, NES Womens Hostel, is located in Guntur city, approximately 10 km from the campus, with 68 rooms (400 students) and an additional facility accommodating 250 students. Each girls' hostel room houses eight students with two attached bathrooms. Hostel fees are approximately INR 43,000 per year for both hostels, payable via Demand Draft (DD) to 'Nagarjuna Education Society Hostels - Men's Hostel Receipts A/c' for boys and 'NES Womens Hostel' for girls, both at Union Bank, Guntur. Bus transportation for girls from Guntur to the college costs INR 18,000 annually (2024-25), payable to RVRJCCE. Hostel timings include a daily schedule with breakfast (7:30-8:30 AM), lunch (12:30-2:00 PM), snacks with tea/milk (4:00-5:00 PM), and dinner (7:30-9:00 PM). Food types include vegetarian meals with milk/coffee at breakfast, tea/milk at snacks, and a variety of South Indian and North Indian dishes. Facilities include computer centers, reading rooms, TV rooms, indoor games (chess, carrom), gym, volleyball and shuttle courts, dispensary with free medicines, mineral water plant, solar hot water, and 24/7 security with CCTV and biometric monitoring. Strict discipline is enforced, with rules prohibiting electronic appliances (e.g., heaters), requiring biometric entry/exit, and mandating adherence to mess and hostel schedules. Hostel committees, headed by conveners (Dr. B. Varaprasad Rao for boys, contact: 0863-2244116; girls' hostel office: 0863-2238171), oversee operations. Want to know about specific hostel rules or campus facilities? Want to dive into specific placement details or campus life?
